@@ -0,0 +1,121 @@
+# MeshAgent authentication specification
+
+This document defines the MeshAgent-specific authentication behavior carried by
+the MeshAgent Codex distribution. The installed executable and app-server
+component retain the upstream names `codex` and `codex-app-server`.
+
+## Credential domains
+
+MeshAgent and OpenAI credentials are independent. MeshAgent credentials use the
+same multi-account store as the MeshAgent CLI, `~/.meshagent/settings.json`.
+OpenAI credentials continue to use Codex's `auth.json` beneath
+`MESHAGENT_CODEX_HOME`. A user may therefore be signed in to both services at
+the same time, and logging in to either service must not remove credentials for
+the other.
+
+The MeshAgent store is a typed, version-compatible representation of the
+MeshAgent CLI settings. Each saved user retains its profile, API URL, OAuth
+session, active project, API-key selections, and LLM proxy token. A successful
+login adds or updates the authenticated user and makes that user active without
+removing other saved users.
+
+## CLI contract
+
+`codex login` and any first-run interactive login default to MeshAgent.
+
+Supported commands are:
+
+```text
+codex login
+codex login --api-url URL
+codex login --provider=meshagent [--api-url URL]
+codex login --provider=openai
+codex login --provider=openai --device-auth
+codex login --provider=openai --with-api-key
+codex login --provider=openai --with-access-token
+codex login status [--provider=meshagent|openai]
+codex login switch [ACCOUNT]
+codex project list
+codex project activate [PROJECT]
+codex logout
+codex logout --provider=meshagent
+codex logout --provider=openai
+```
+
+`ACCOUNT` accepts the saved MeshAgent user ID, email address, or an
+unambiguous display name. When it is omitted on an interactive terminal, Codex
+shows a picker. A non-interactive invocation without `ACCOUNT` lists the saved
+accounts, with the active account marked, matching the MeshAgent Rust CLI.
+Switching changes the active saved user without starting OAuth.
+
+`codex project list` lists projects available to the active MeshAgent account
+and marks its active project. `codex project activate PROJECT` accepts a project
+ID, project key, exact project name, or unambiguous case-insensitive project
+name. If `PROJECT` is omitted on an interactive terminal, Codex shows a picker.
+Project selection is stored on the active MeshAgent account.
+
+`--api-url` applies only to MeshAgent login and is rejected for OpenAI login or
+for `status` and `switch`. Resolution follows the MeshAgent CLI precedence:
+the explicit flag, `MESHAGENT_API_URL`, the active profile's saved API URL, and
+finally `https://api.meshagent.com`. The resolved URL is normalized and saved
+with the authenticated profile.
+
+OpenAI-only credential flags require `--provider=openai`; they never silently
+change the default provider.
+
+`codex logout --provider=meshagent` clears the active MeshAgent user's session,
+matching `meshagent auth logout`, while retaining saved profiles and other
+users. `codex logout --provider=openai` invokes the existing Codex logout and
+does not alter MeshAgent settings. Unqualified `codex logout` attempts both
+operations and reports their combined result. MCP OAuth credentials remain
+managed by `codex mcp logout`.
+
+## OAuth and session behavior
+
+MeshAgent login uses authorization-code OAuth with PKCE S256, a random state,
+and the MeshAgent CLI callback `http://localhost:8765/callback`. Codex validates
+the state before exchanging the code at `/oauth/token`, resolves the user at
+`/accounts/profiles/me`, and persists the resulting session. The OAuth client,
+scope, and API URL retain the MeshAgent CLI environment overrides.
+
+Access tokens refresh when their stored expiration is within five minutes.
+Refresh uses the OAuth refresh-token grant and persists rotated refresh tokens.
+An unauthorized model request forces one refresh before the request is retried.
+
+## Project and model routing
+
+The distribution includes a built-in `meshagent` model provider and selects it
+when no model provider is explicitly configured. OpenAI remains available as
+the built-in `openai` provider. Signing in does not itself switch an explicitly
+configured model provider.
+
+MeshAgent requests use the active profile's API URL with `/openai/v1`, attach
+the active OAuth bearer token, and send the active project as
+`Meshagent-Project-Id`. Login preserves a valid existing project, selects the
+only available project automatically, or asks the user to choose when multiple
+projects are available. A missing project is reported before model execution.
+
+## Interactive and app-server behavior
+
+First-run TUI onboarding presents MeshAgent as the default sign-in method and
+uses the same login, storage, refresh, and project-selection implementation.
+OpenAI login remains available explicitly through
+`codex login --provider=openai`. The existing app-server OpenAI account RPC
+remains independent from MeshAgent's shared settings, while the app-server
+model provider resolves MeshAgent credentials for model requests. One
+credential domain therefore cannot hide or delete the other.
+
+The TUI `/project` command opens a project picker for the active MeshAgent
+account. A selection updates shared settings and the model-provider configuration
+used by subsequent turns. It never changes the project of an in-flight turn.
+
+The OAuth callback listener is temporary and belongs to the invoking Codex
+process. It does not create or join a shared daemon or process group.
+
+## Verification
+
+Tests must cover provider/flag validation, API URL precedence, OAuth state and
+PKCE handling, token refresh and rotation, multi-account persistence and
+switching, per-account projects, independent login and targeted logout, model
+request headers, unauthorized retry, and TUI onboarding behavior. Network tests
+use local mock servers only.
